---
// src/pages/legal/cookie-notice.astro
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Notice"
  description="How this website uses cookies and similar technologies, and how to control them. This is a static site with no analytics, advertising, or cross-site tracking."
  updated="30 July 2026"
  intro="This site is built to be quiet. It uses as little tracking as it is possible to use."
>
  <h2>What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files a website can store in your browser. Similar technologies
    include local storage, session storage, and tracking pixels. They are used to remember
    settings, to keep a site secure, and sometimes to measure how a site is used.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site uses</h2>
  <p>This website is a static site. It does not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Set advertising or cross-site tracking cookies</li>
    <li>Run analytics software of any kind</li>
    <li>Embed social media buttons, trackers, or pixels</li>
    <li>Load fonts, scripts, or images from third-party servers — typefaces are served from our own domain</li>
    <li>Build a profile of you or your browsing</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may set a small number of strictly necessary cookies to keep the
    site secure and available — for example, to balance server load, to protect the
    contact form against automated abuse, and to detect malicious traffic. These are used
    only to operate the site and cannot be used to identify you across other websites.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because we set no non-essential cookies, no consent banner is required and none is
    shown. We consider that a feature.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party giving platforms</h2>
  <p>
    Our Partner page links to outside giving services. When you follow one of those links,
    you leave this website and the receiving service sets its own cookies under its own
    policies. We do not control those cookies and receive no information from them. Review
    each provider’s privacy and cookie policies before giving.
  </p>

  <h2>If we ever add analytics</h2>
  <p>
    If we later add analytics, a giving form hosted directly on this site, embedded video,
    or a mailing-list signup, we will update this notice before or at the time those tools
    go live, name the provider, describe what is collected, and add a consent mechanism
    where one is required.
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can view, delete, and block cookies through your browser settings. Blocking
    strictly necessary cookies may affect form submission or site security features. Help
    pages for the major browsers explain how.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some browsers send a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal. Because this site
    does not track visitors across other websites and does not sell or share personal
    information, there is nothing for such a signal to switch off. We would honor one if
    that ever changed.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this notice. The date at the top reflects the current version.
  </p>

  <h2>More information</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle
    information you send us, or write to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
